+---
+title: Testing click.utils to full line+branch coverage
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 53191 }
+touches:
+  - tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py
+  - src/click/utils.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- Extra click.utils tests live in tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py; with them the full suite covers src/click/utils.py at 100% lines and branches.
+- Platform branches in get_app_dir are tested by monkeypatching click.utils.WIN and sys.platform, so they run identically on any OS.
+- _expand_args's `except re.error` branch is reached by monkeypatching glob.glob (it is imported inside the function, so patching the glob module works).
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Relying on a real invalid glob pattern to raise re.error: modern Python's glob/fnmatch doesn't reliably raise, so patch instead.
+
+## Watch out
+- pyproject sets filterwarnings = "error": accessing deprecated click.utils names (LazyFile, safecall, ...) without pytest.warns fails the test; import the underscore-prefixed names instead.
+- echo() probes a file with write(b"") and then write("") (_compat._is_binary_writer). A fake file used to hit the "bytes but no binary writer" path must reject b"" and will also receive "" — filter that when asserting.
+- _LazyFile("-", "r") reads sys.stdin; under pytest stdin is unreadable, so monkeypatch sys.stdin with io.TextIOWrapper(io.BytesIO(...)).
